Please note that this position is based in Berlin, London or Paris depending on your availability.&nbsp; 
 &nbsp;
 THE BEST WORK OF YOUR CAREER &nbsp; 
 Trade Republic is the largest savings platform in Europe - we operate in 18 countries, serving +10 million customers who trusted us with over 150B in assets. But we’re striving for more.
We have a bold mission to empower everyone to build wealth with easy, safe, and free access to financial systems. You will have the opportunity to grow your career by collaborating with a team of outstanding talents and state of the art technology to build a lasting, positive future for millions.
 &nbsp;
 &nbsp;
 WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING
 We are looking for Product Managers of different seniority levels in several product areas, such as Banking, Cards, Wealth. Your responsibilities will include:
 Become the ultimate owner of one or more products, taking care of them from ideation to delivery, engineering team management, tracking performance and business impact
 Analyze data to find the right problems to solve, and breaking solutions down into smaller executable chunks that deliver value
 Understand your user and existing state-of-the-art solutions, and create a compelling product vision and roadmap
 Work cross-functionally with engineers and operations managers, and interact security, compliance, data, and legal teams to craft solutions that will delight our users and provide value to the business
 &nbsp;
 WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR
 Minimum 4 years of product management hands-on experience in user facing products 
 Founder-mindset - you enjoy working in highly autonomous, ambiguous and fast paced environment 
 Strong analytical, prioritization, organisational and problem solving skills 
 Experience in successfully working with cross-functional teams (engineering, data, security, operations, design 
 &nbsp;
 WHY YOU SHOULD APPLY NOW
 Our culture rewards ownership, excellence, and high energy. We care deeply about outcomes and hold each other accountable - we’re here to win and fix one of the largest challenges Europeans face - closing the pension gap and democratising wealth. If this gets you fired up, reach out!
 We believe it’s our team’s varied identities and backgrounds that make us sharper and stronger. We’re committed to creating an environment where everyone feels respected and has equal opportunity to thrive in their careers. For any questions on DEI during the interview process, reach out to your recruitment partner.

Build the Market Leader in Satellite Analytics with us at LiveEO
 At LiveEO, we combine Space Technology with AI to solve problems here on Earth. Our satellite-based monitoring solutions help Infrastructure operators and industrial companies to make their operations more ecological, safer, and more efficient.
LiveEO is applying the latest developments in artificial intelligence to analyse satellite data and is bringing the insights of earth observation data to customers in the enterprise sector. LiveEO’s ambitious goal is to monitor 1 billion assets across the globe with its unique SaaS solution until 2030. Our team is as global as the satellite data we process and the customers we serve. Together, we are building something big.
We’re looking for a Senior Project Manager to lead the delivery of our geospatial and satellite-imagery projects. You’ll make sure every project is delivered to specification, on time and on budget. Just as importantly, you’ll make sure it solves the customer’s real problems and delivers measurable results.
 Your challenge
 Customer delivery
 Scope management: define and confirm areas of interest, deliverables, data requirements and acceptance criteria with the customer; control scope changes and change requests;
 Schedule management: plan and track timelines that account for satellite acquisition windows, weather/cloud cover, data availability and processing lead times;
 Cost management: plan and control project budgets, including imagery/data procurement and processing costs;
 Quality management: set quality benchmarks and acceptance criteria for geospatial deliverables; coordinate quality assurance and quality control and drive resolution of findings;
 Resource management: plan and negotiate capacity across cross-functional teams;
 Risk management: identify, assess and mitigate delivery risks (e.g. data acquisition, customer input data, processing, accuracy); build contingency plans;
 Procurement & third-party management: coordinate with data and imagery providers and other external suppliers;
 Stakeholder & communications management: manage expectations of customer and internal stakeholders at all levels, including senior decision makers; provide clear, regular status reporting;
 Lessons learned & continuous improvement: capture learnings after each project and shape delivery methodology and good practices.
 Technical account management
 Participate in customer calls and communicate details of LiveEO's technical capabilities to the interested customer, help to set and manage expectations;
 Build a deep understanding of the customer's business, operational processes, systems, data and pain points;
 Apply a value framework to articulate how the delivered solution addresses each customer pain point and what measurable value it creates;
 Act as the trusted technical counterpart for the customer throughout the delivery and beyond, ensuring adoption of the delivered solution;
 Feed customer insights and recurring pain points back to product and commercial teams;
 Create technical presentations demonstrating how our product meets client needs.
 Your profile
 Must have:
 5+ years in project management, sales engineering or professional services engineering, with a degree in business, IT, geoinformatics, remote sensing, surveying or engineering;
 Proven end-to-end delivery of complex projects: planning, risk assessment and contingency planning across interdependent workstreams, grounded in agile practices;
 Experience managing senior customer stakeholders, including negotiating scope, timelines and change requests, with a strong drive to engage directly with customers in professional working English;
 Track record of shaping delivery methodology and good practices, and of building reports and dashboards that make project status and performance visible and drive improvement;
 Leads by influence rather than authority, and works independently, reliably and efficiently;
 Hands-on experience with GIS solutions; previous experience in the earth observation or GIS industry is a plus
 Daily, hands-on use of AI tools and agents (e.g. Claude, ChatGPT) to speed up planning, reporting, analysis and documentation.
 Nice to have:
 Knowledge of satellite technology and knowledge of ML and DL algorithms;
 Working knowledge in a modern programming language, preferably Python;
 Professional Project Management Certification from accredited institution;
 Domain knowledge in utility vegetation management, transmission & distribution or rail asset data (e.g. PLS-CADD), LiDAR or photogrammetry;
 Other language skills.
 Your Benefits
 Gain direct insights into and influence strategic business decisions shaping our go-to-market (GTM) strategy, while working on cutting-edge SaaS and AI solutions that enhance business processes and lives globally.
 Join a rapidly growing multinational leader in an evolving and impactful industry, surrounded by a talented, international team of experts from 30+ nationalities.
 Flexible working hours - we trust our employees to get their work done while maintaining a healthy work-life balance
 Enjoy significant responsibility with the autonomy to drive change, shape processes, and innovate. We encourage career development, creativity, and bold ideas.
 Benefit from a culture of continuous learning, with frequent internal workshops, knowledge-sharing sessions, journal clubs, and hackathons.
 Receive fair remuneration with the opportunity to participate in company ownership through our VESOP (Virtual Employee Stock Option Plan).
 Wellness, life insurance and other benefits
 At LiveEO, we value diverse backgrounds and experiences. We encourage anyone with a strong profile to apply, regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, or religion.
